Why not just use a parallel for with static partitioning instead? #pragma omp parallel shared(dx) num_threads(t)
{
   double x = omp_get_thread_num() * 1.0 / t;

   #pragma omp for reduction(+ : parallel_Sum) 
   for (int i = 0; i < num_steps; ++i)
   {     
       parallel_Sum += 4.0*dx/(1.0+x*x);
       x += dx;
   }
} Then you won't need to manage all the partitioning and atomic collection of results by yourself. In order to correctly initialize x , we notice that x = (begin * dx) = (threadIdx * num_steps/t) * (1.0 / num_steps) = (threadIdx * 1.0) / t . Edit : Just tested this final version on my machine and it seems to work correctly.

